            {
              "id": "exabeam_context_table_trigger",
              "name": "ExabeamContextTableTrigger",
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#exabeam_context_table_trigger",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A sequence whose query looks a value up in a context table has a threshold."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A sequence whose query looks a value up in a context table has a threshold."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "exabeam_context_table_trigger\n\nA sequence whose query looks a value up in a context table has a threshold.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate on an exabeam block (exabeam-1.0). Exabeam requires \"Trigger on first match\" for a sequence with a context table lookup (user IN \"Privileged Accounts\"), so the sequence takes no threshold.\n\nExample\n\nsequences:\n  - query: activity_type:\"app-login\" AND user IN \"Privileged Accounts\"\n    threshold:\n      function: count\n      operator: more_than\n      value: 5\n      within: 1h\n\nHow to fix\n\nRemove the threshold, or move the lookup to a sequence of its own that triggers on any match and correlate the two.",
                "markdown": "# exabeam_context_table_trigger\n\nA sequence whose query looks a value up in a context table has a threshold.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` on an `exabeam` block (exabeam-1.0). Exabeam requires \"Trigger on first match\" for a sequence with a context table lookup (`user IN \"Privileged Accounts\"`), so the sequence takes no `threshold`.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nsequences:\n  - query: activity_type:\"app-login\" AND user IN \"Privileged Accounts\"\n    threshold:\n      function: count\n      operator: more_than\n      value: 5\n      within: 1h\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nRemove the `threshold`, or move the lookup to a sequence of its own that triggers on any match and correlate the two.\n"
