              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "`opentide new` would write a file that already exists, and it never overwrites one."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "path_exists\n\nopentide new would write a file that already exists, and it never overwrites one.\n\nExit 1, as failure.code. Raised when --path names an existing file, or when a file appears at the chosen path while new runs.\n\nExample\n\nopentide new threat --name \"Credential Dumping\" --path objects/threats/credential-dumping.yaml\n\nHow to fix\n\nPass another --path, or leave --path out: without it, new appends -<uuid[:8]> to the file name when the name is taken. To start over, delete or move the existing file first.",
                "markdown": "# path_exists\n\n`opentide new` would write a file that already exists, and it never overwrites one.\n\nExit 1, as `failure.code`. Raised when `--path` names an existing file, or when a file appears at the chosen path while `new` runs.\n\n## Example\n\n```text\nopentide new threat --name \"Credential Dumping\" --path objects/threats/credential-dumping.yaml\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nPass another `--path`, or leave `--path` out: without it, `new` appends `-<uuid[:8]>` to the file name when the name is taken. To start over, delete or move the existing file first.\n"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "path_not_writable",
              "name": "PathNotWritable",
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#path_not_writable",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "`opentide new` could not create the folder or the file it scaffolds, because the operating system refused the write: a read-only checkout, a folder another user owns, or a full disk."
