            {
              "id": "yaral_section_empty",
              "name": "YaralSectionEmpty",
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_empty",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section key is present with no text."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section key is present with no text."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "yaral_section_empty\n\nA YARA-L section key is present with no text.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). The key loaded as YAML null or blank text, or as a YAML list or mapping instead of text. A plain YAML scalar that starts with # is a YAML comment, so condition: #fail > 3 loads as null.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: #e > 5\n\nHow to fix\n\nWrite each section as a block scalar (|), which YAML keeps verbatim:\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: |\n      #e > 5",
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_empty\n\nA YARA-L section key is present with no text.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). The key loaded as YAML `null` or blank text, or as a YAML list or mapping instead of text. A plain YAML scalar that starts with `#` is a YAML comment, so `condition: #fail > 3` loads as null.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: #e > 5\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nWrite each section as a block scalar (`|`), which YAML keeps verbatim:\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    condition: |\n      #e > 5\n```\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "yaral_section_header",
              "name": "YaralSectionHeader",
              "helpUri": "https://opentide.org/docs/cli/diagnostics#yaral_section_header",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule` header or a rule's braces."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule` header or a rule's braces."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "yaral_section_header\n\nA YARA-L section text holds a section label, a rule header or a rule's braces.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by opentide validate (its schema check) on a configurations.google_secops block (yara-l-1.0). Each section is its own key, and deploy writes the rule <name> { header, the meta section and the labels itself. A label or a header inside a comment or a string does not count.\n\nExample\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      rule office_powershell {\n        events:\n          $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n        condition:\n          $e\n      }\n\nHow to fix\n\nMove each section's lines under its own key and drop the header, meta and braces:\n\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n    condition: |\n      $e",
                "markdown": "# yaral_section_header\n\nA YARA-L section text holds a section label, a `rule` header or a rule's braces.\n\nSeverity: error. Reported by `opentide validate` (its `schema` check) on a `configurations.google_secops` block (yara-l-1.0). Each section is its own key, and deploy writes the `rule <name> {` header, the `meta` section and the labels itself. A label or a header inside a comment or a string does not count.\n\n## Example\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      rule office_powershell {\n        events:\n          $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n        condition:\n          $e\n      }\n```\n\n## How to fix\n\nMove each section's lines under its own key and drop the header, `meta` and braces:\n\n```yaml\nconfigurations:\n  google_secops:\n    events: |\n      $e.metadata.event_type = \"PROCESS_LAUNCH\"\n    condition: |\n      $e\n```\n"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              }
            },
            {
